course: dictionary
lesson: 10096
title: Thicken and the plot thickens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To thicken means to become thicker, or to make something thicker. A runny liquid thickens when it becomes less runny, like sauce or custard. Fog, smoke or a crowd can also thicken, which means it becomes denser.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Friendly bacteria thicken the milk and make it tangy.» The milk is changing into something less runny, so thicken means become thicker. Check by swapping in "become thicker": the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Thicken also has a story meaning. «The plot thickens» means the story is becoming more mysterious and complicated, like a detective finding a new clue. Nothing is getting physically thicker here, so always check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: To thicken means to become thicker, or to make something thicker.
fact: Liquids, fog, smoke and crowds can all thicken, meaning they become denser.
fact: «The plot thickens» means a story becomes more mysterious and complicated.
fact: «Thicken» is used in cooking, when heating custard or adding flour to a sauce.
fact: A good check is to swap in "became thicker" or "became more complicated" and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Friendly bacteria thicken the milk and make it tangy.» What does thicken mean here? | *Become less runny and thicker | Shrink into a smaller pot | Become colder and wetter | Turn a different colour
exercise: In a story, «The plot thickens» means what? | *The story becomes more mysterious and complicated | Someone is cooking a thick stew | The book gets heavier and longer | The ending is happy and simple
exercise: Which of these can thicken, meaning become denser? | Sunshine | Laughter | *Fog | Sneezes
exercise: The smoke thickened over the town. What does thickened mean? | Became lighter and clearer | Cleared away quickly | *Became denser | Turned bright blue
exercise: Ella says the mystery plot thickened in chapter three. What does it mean? | The book became heavier | The pages were torn | *The story got more complicated | The story got less exciting
test: «Mum's sauce was too runny, so she added flour and let it thicken.» What does thicken mean here? | Become colder | Become sweeter | *Become thicker | Spill over the edge
test: Butterworts have sticky leaves, and in Scandinavia their leaves were once used to thicken milk. What does thicken mean? | Pour milk into a cup | Make milk turn sour | *Make milk thicker | Freeze the milk solid
exam: «The fog thickened as the boats sailed out.» What does the fog do? | Lifts up into the sky | Clears away quickly | Turns into rain | *Becomes denser and harder to see through
